From 3fd7f6ecea7dd9c79c85c315e2dd5e6980e077ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 11:16:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch: guard openssl.path() when the openssl CLI is absent

IvorySQL 3.0 (an early PG16 fork) calls `openssl.path()` unconditionally in
`src/test/ssl/meson.build`, which aborts `meson setup` with "Unable to get the
path of a not-found external program" when the openssl binary is absent (the
hermetic sandbox ships none). Upstream PostgreSQL guards it as
`openssl.found() ? openssl.path() : ''`, and IvorySQL 4.0/5.0 carry that guard;
backport it so the `--enable-tap-tests` test variant can configure. The ssl
suite skips without PG_TEST_EXTRA, so the empty value is never read.

References: https://postgr.es/c/b64c8b01c2
References: https://postgr.es/c/2a08dda291
---
 src/test/ssl/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/test/ssl/meson.build b/src/test/ssl/meson.build
index 4cda81f3bc..abb30ab214 100644
--- a/src/test/ssl/meson.build
+++ b/src/test/ssl/meson.build
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ tests += {
   'tap': {
     'env': {
       'with_ssl': ssl_library,
-      'OPENSSL': openssl.path(),
+      'OPENSSL': openssl.found() ? openssl.path() : '',
     },
     'tests': [
       't/001_ssltests.pl',
